  "body": "**Link to problem area**:\n\nC-S API:\n\n- [`m.room.third_party_invite`](https://spec.matrix.org/v1.13/client-server-api/#mroomthird_party_invite)\n\nIS API:\n\n- [`POST /_matrix/identity/v2/store-invite`](https://spec.matrix.org/v1.13/identity-service-api/#post_matrixidentityv2store-invite)\n- [`GET /_matrix/identity/v2/pubkey/ephemeral/isvalid`](https://spec.matrix.org/v1.13/identity-service-api/#get_matrixidentityv2pubkeyephemeralisvalid)\n- [`GET /_matrix/identity/v2/pubkey/{keyId}`](https://spec.matrix.org/v1.13/identity-service-api/#get_matrixidentityv2pubkeykeyid)\n\n**Issue**\n\nThe documentation of the `public_key` and `public_keys` fields issued by identity servers mention unpadded base64, the one from the IS API even linking to the definition in the appendices using standard base64.\n\nHowever Sydent sends the long-term public key encoded using standard base64 and the ephemeral public key encoded as URL-safe base64 (as can be seen in https://github.com/matrix-org/sydent/pull/10). So this documentation should be clarified to say that both standard and URL-safe base64 can be expected for those fields.\n\nRelated: #838.",
